            <div xml:id="d684">

                <pb facs="0806" n="704" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg704"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 25818.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of Embassy Schuyler to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-04-25"><hi rendition="#italic">April 25,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 265.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that the
                    convention for the preservation of the status quo in the Baltic was signed at
                    the ministry for foreign affairs on April 23 by Mr. Iswolsky, minister for
                    foreign affairs, and by the representatives of Germany, Sweden, and Denmark.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Montgomery
                    Schuyler.</hi></signed></closer>



